<title>PERU: Peru's October silver output falls 0.70 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru's October silver output falls 0.70 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's silver output fell 0.70 percent to 162,064 tonnes in October, compared with the same month last year, according to preliminary figures from the Energy and Mines Ministry released Monday.</p>
<p>Production rose 2.34 percent to 1.606 million tonnes in the first ten months of the year, compared with the same period last year, the ministry said.</p>
<p>Peru is the world's number two silver producer after Mexico. State-owned mining company Centromin Peru is the country's largest producer.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Cawthorne, Lima newsroom 511 221-2134</p>
</text>
